{#
compose/_sent.stream.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The cancel window is over: the message is where it belongs, the composer is
gone, and a toast says so.

Rendered when the composer asks for it (ComposeController::sent(), driven by
compose--compose#_settleSend) and when a cancel arrives too late to take —
both are the same fact, "this message has gone", and they must leave the same
page behind.

Everything here used to happen the instant the send was accepted, which is
what made the window's own pill useless as a cancel surface: it was not on
screen any more. Deferring it by the cancel window is the whole shape of this
round.

**The conversation is only touched when it is the conversation on screen**,
and that condition is not decoration — it is the forward bug. A reply is
filed in the thread it answers, so `ctx.thread` (the thread the composer was
opened against) and the sent message's thread are the same and the message can
simply join the conversation below. A FORWARD starts a new conversation: the
sent message lands in a thread that is nowhere on the page, so the three
streams below addressed `thread_messages_…` and `reply_zone_…` ids that did
not exist, every one of them was silently dropped, and the composer sat there
saying "Sending…" for ever. Closing the frame is therefore unconditional and
comes first; the conversation is updated only when there is one to update.

A forward's mail is not shown anywhere on this page as a result, because it is
not part of this conversation — it is in Sent, and the toast is what says it
went.

Variables: message, thread (MessageThread|null), ctx, notify (default true)
#}
{# The too-late answer includes this template for the tidying and brings its
   own toast — an error one, which is the news that matters there. Two toasts
   stacked, one saying the send failed to stop and one saying it went, is the
   same fact told twice with the second half burying the first. #}
{% set notify = notify|default(true) %}
{# Is the sent message part of the conversation this composer was opened in?
   Both halves are needed: the dock carries `thread` too (a reply opened below
   md lands there), and a message can have no thread at all. #}
{% set inConversation = thread is not null and ctx.thread is not null and thread.id == ctx.thread %}

{# The composer goes, wherever it was. For an inline window that frame IS the
   window's root; for the dock it is the dock. Emptying it disconnects
   compose--compose, which is what gives a thread its Reply / Forward buttons
   back — see the `composing` class in app.css. #}
<turbo-stream action="update" target="{{ ctx.frame }}">
    <template></template>
</turbo-stream>

{% if inConversation %}
    {# The draft's row is already in the conversation — hidden while the editor
       was open — so it is dropped and the sent message re-appended at the end,
       which is where it now belongs. #}
    <turbo-stream action="remove" target="thread_message_{{ message.id }}">
    </turbo-stream>

    <turbo-stream action="append" target="thread_messages_{{ thread.id }}">
        <template>
            {% include 'mail/_thread_message.html.twig' with { message: message, expanded: true, draft: false } only %}
        </template>
    </turbo-stream>

    {# Redrawn without the composer and without the countdown bar this used to
       carry: the pill was the only cancel there was, and it is spent. #}
    <turbo-stream action="replace" target="reply_zone_{{ thread.id }}">
        <template>
            {% include 'mail/_reply_zone.html.twig' with { thread: thread } only %}
        </template>
    </turbo-stream>
{% endif %}

{# The one piece of feedback the send gets that is not the button itself.
   Without it a mail sent from the dock was a window that simply vanished, and
   a forward was a composer that closed with nothing said at all. #}
{% if notify %}
    <turbo-stream action="append" target="toast-region">
        <template>
            {% include '_partials/_toast.html.twig' with {
                type: 'success',
                message: 'toast.sent'|trans,
            } only %}
        </template>
    </turbo-stream>
{% endif %}
